        "timestamp": 1776808232,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. 'Landmark' EU court ruling rejects Hungary anti-LGBTQ law Europe Issued on: 21/04/2026 - 23:50 The EU's top court ruled Tuesday that anti-LGBTQ legislation in Hungary breached the bloc's rules, in a move hailed as a \"landmark\" victory by Brussels. The European Commission, 16 of 27 member states and the European Parliament took Hungary to the European Court of Justice (ECJ) over the law, in what has been billed as the largest human rights case in the bloc's history. FRANCE 24's James Vasina reports. Russia's Sergei Shoigu says safety of Russians in Transnistria under threat, TASS reports 21/04/2026 Europe Significant 'overlap' between auto industry and arms manufacturing, expert says 21/04/2026 Europe 'Mood shifting' in Europe: Public opinion and governments 'turning against Israel' 21/04/2026 Middle East Jet fuel prices flying sky high 21/04/2026 Europe Full suspension of trade relations with Israel requires EU unanimity 21/04/2026 Europe EU pushes to limit carry-on bag fees 21/04/2026 Europe EU hosts Palestinian peace conference 21/04/2026 Middle East EU mulls ending trade agreement with Israel over human rights concerns 21/04/2026 Europe 'Unprecedented since 1999': Radev secures absolute majority with reformist and eurosceptic coalition 20/04/2026 Europe"
